{
  "sheet": "spells",
  "about": "Noita projectile spells as new Magicraft spells. Each one has its own id and ability type (Magicraft resolves a spell in a wand by ability type), so its name, icon, stats and behavior are its own. Every Noita number (speed, lifetime, damage and damage types, bounces, bounce energy, low-speed death, friction or acceleration, piercing, wall collision, explosion radius/damage, cast delay, spread, crit, mana, price) is read at runtime from the player's Noita (gun_actions.lua and the projectile XML it adds) and turned into Magicraft numbers with scaling.json. Visuals (projectile sprite and animation, trail material colour, explosion sprite, bounce effect) and sounds (decoded from Noita's projectiles.bank) also come from the player's Noita. Noita's gravity is left out: Magicraft is top-down.",
  "columns": {
    "noitaId": "Noita action id in gun_actions.lua",
    "newBase": "4-digit id for the new spell (ids newBase*10+level, ability type newBase); first digit 1, not used by Magicraft",
    "rarity": "Common | Rare | Epic (Magicraft drop rarity)",
    "copies": "projectiles per cast (Noita adds several for some spells, e.g. Triplicate bolt)",
    "special": "none | teleport (caster moves to where it ends) | blackhole (pulls enemies, damages over time) | beam (draws a line from the caster) | thrown (no Noita speed: uses throwSpeed)",
    "throwSpeed": "Noita px/s used when the projectile has no speed of its own (thrown/physics items); 0 = use Noita's",
    "shootSound": "Noita projectiles.bank sound name prefix played on cast (a random numbered variant)",
    "hitSound": "sound prefix when it hits an enemy or ends (bank:prefix; bank is projectiles or explosion)",
    "bounceSound": "sound prefix on each wall bounce, or none",
    "why": "what Noita's spell does, as built here"
  },
